meta {
  name: Agent Session Actions - Decide
  type: http
  seq: 30
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/public/v1/agents/:agent/sessions/:session/actions/decisions
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{apiKey}}
}

params:path {
  agent: {{agentId}}
  session: {{agentSessionId}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "decisions": [
      {
        "action_id": "{{agentActionId}}",
        "decision": "approve",
        "note": "Approved by the integration."
      }
    ]
  }
}

docs {
  Decides a conversation's waiting actions. Requires the `agents:invoke`
  ability on the key — the key is the approver.

  - `decisions` — required, 1 to 100 entries, each with `action_id`
    (uuid), `decision` (`approve`, `edit` or `reject`), `arguments`
    (required for `edit`), and optional `note` (max 2000) and `stop`.
    `remember` is accepted but always ignored here.

  Any `action_id` not in this conversation answers `404`. An action whose
  tool names its own approvers can only be decided by them in the app —
  `403`. Actions no longer pending are skipped; decided turns resume on
  the queue (poll `Agent Sessions - Get`).

  Response is wrapped: `{ success, statusCode, message, data: { actions } }`.
}
